== Review (by hand, 9 Nov)
Section 0: the five calls in loop conditions are the B0-B2 ones reviewed on 8 Nov; tb_router.sv's two moved
by 8 lines with B4's tie-offs (475 -> 483, 596 -> 604). B4's code has none: wait_delivered computes
sb_pkg::outstanding() before its loop (D41). Every line that declares or uses a simulation-only hook
(tb_hold, the turn and coverage counters) is under `ifndef SYNTHESIS and outside the synthesis-off pragmas,
so every simulator keeps it and synthesis drops it (section 6 converts the RTL with sv2v -DSYNTHESIS).
Section 3: BP05's counts of several-packet bursts and of packets taken from mesh inputs are coverage goals
(tb_pkg::cover_goal): a short run may miss one (4x4 with +QUICK at seeds 4 and 12 has no several-packet
burst) and then prints an INFO line instead of failing; BP02 and BP04 make both happen on purpose. BP05
lasts at least one timetable round (8x8: 10,332 cycles; 4x4 and 2x2 keep their lengths).
Design A, full form, run separately on the section-2 binary: tb_mesh on 4x4, N01-N04 and N06-N08 in one run,
RESULT N01-N08 PASS checks=46273022 in 1,231,461 cycles (174 s), the README count; with +QUICK in one run
444,704 checks in 14,811 cycles.
Section 4: TEST_U05's MULTITOP lines are one warning (three lines), as in B2 and B3: the design pane's modules
a test does not use are extra tops (README Section 3); the testbench pane adds only the chosen test's top.
Section 6: bypass_source is 20,472 generic cells for 37 flip-flops. Most of it is select logic: each of the
20 steps of the rotating scan reads rdy, dst and len through a 20-way variable index (about 10,000 cells), and
the flit for crossbar input 4 goes through a 20-way, 134-bit mux (about 5,000). A 5-bit sum instead of int
saves only 946 cells (19,535). Design B's router is 62,326 cells against design A's 38,280 (flip-flops
15,658 against 15,450). Function is not affected; the area matters for E11 and is raised as an issue.

== Fix after the xsim runs (9 Nov)
R-1109-01 and R-1109-03 (xsim 2024.2) passed with the Verilator counts, and every output line matched but one:
BP05's count of packets taken from mesh inputs (its INFO and COVER lines) was garbage on xsim
(1911612530959056942 for 46 on 4x4, 16129901137854726251 for 107 on 2x2). Riviera-PRO (R-1109-BP05) and
Verilator agree. The simulation-only counter n_remote in bypass_source.sv added $countones(take[15:0]); it now
adds n_take_mesh, counted with a loop (README Section 2, rule 9; the pre-check scans for $countones of a bit
range: none left). Checks after the fix:
  sv2v -DSYNTHESIS of the whole RTL is byte-identical before and after: no synthesizable logic changed
  RTL lint of bypass_source, 48 sets (NUM_VC 1-4, MESH_N 2-16, B_MAX 5/10/15), and of the router: clean
  tb_mesh_b 4x4, 2x2 and 8x8 rebuilt with -Wall: clean; their output (4x4 all, 2x2 all, 8x8 +TEST=BP02,
  4x4 +TEST=BP05 +QUICK) is identical, line for line, to the runs before the fix
  EDA bundle regenerated: only design_part2.sv changed; +define+TEST_BP05 +QUICK from it gives the same lines
Every other xsim and Riviera-PRO line equals Verilator's, except that tb_router (R-1109-04) prints the lines of
its four parallel testers in another order (the same lines, as since B1).
